@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s33a-credit-point`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] — ss 34, 36 and 36A: the three personal
-- credit points that carry no condition beyond who the taxpayer is. Row IL-01.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt
--   (sha256 b87f2cf4...b81b6; "line N" is a line of that file). Hebrew is
--   authoritative; quotations are rendered mechanically by render_source.py.
--
-- Each section is one sentence: "In computing the tax of <a person of this
-- kind>, <so many> credit points shall be taken into account." Each is
-- encoded twice over:
--   * `section N, as written, applies to` — the sentence's own limbs, nothing
--     else, so a reader can hold the Hebrew beside it;
--   * `section N applies to` — the same, with the two provisions OUTSIDE this
--     row that can change the answer for some people: s 48 (an order may
--     extend ss 34 and 36 to Area residents who are not Israeli citizens) and
--     s 48A (regulations may disapply the Chapter's credits to a foreign
--     worker). Neither is encoded, so where either could decide the case the
--     rule REFUSES, and only there.
-- A person to whom a section does not apply gets no points under it. That is
-- the law's own answer, an ordinary 0, not a refusal.
--
-- None of these is the person's TOTAL of credit points: ss 35, 37-40D, 44-46
-- and others add more (row IL-08), and s 41 and s 66 rework them for spouses
-- (rows IL-08 and IL-02). The aggregates below are named for exactly the
-- sections they add.
--
-- TWO SETS OF RULES (0.2.0).
--   * The year-free rules over a Person (the first part of the module, as in
--     0.1.0): they take no tax year and answer on the deposited text, with
--     s 48A's refusal undated; and since a Person carries only the s 1
--     residence status, they cannot see s 3A(f). They are kept, unchanged,
--     as the building blocks and as the interface the independent tests use.
--   * The year-aware rules over a `Taxpayer in a tax year` (the second part,
--     from `§§ The tax years the deposited text governs`): they refuse a tax
--     year before each section's last listed amendment, apply s 48A's refusal
--     from tax year 2002 (s 48A was enacted in 5763), and route an
--     Israeli citizen who is a resident of, or operates in, the Area through
--     s 3A(f) "as if" an Israeli resident. The @export is among them.
--   * (0.3.0) The year-aware points rules also take the readings of forks F1
--     (s 36A and residence), F2 (s 36 and income from personal exertion)
--     and F4 (residence for part of a tax year), RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08
--     (SHRUG): by default they decline by name where the readings give
--     different answers; each reading is kept by name (`, under the
--     readings`). See `§§ The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Part C, Chapter Three — credits under sections 34, 36 and 36A`

§§ `Reading the facts of the case`

-- Accessors over a Person. A body of persons is not an individual, so every
-- fact an individual carries is FALSE for it.

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is an individual` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a woman` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a woman`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a foreign worker` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an individual` i  THEN i's `a foreign worker`
    WHEN `a body of persons` THEN FALSE

§§ `Sections 48 and 48A — reached, not encoded`

-- line 1807: שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע בצו כי הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37, כולן או מקצתן, יחולו ... גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כולם או חלקם, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל
-- The power has been exercised: the Wikisource note at line 1808 records
-- the Income Tax (Credits for Area Residents) Order 5755-1995, applying
-- ss 34, 36 and 37 to Area residents who are not Israeli citizens "as if
-- they were Israeli residents". The order is not in this row's source
-- bundle and s 48 is outside this row, so where it could decide the case —
-- a non-resident individual who is an Area resident and not an Israeli
-- citizen — the rule refuses. (s 48 does not name s 36A; see fork F1.)
@ref ITO s 48, lines 1806-1808 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- line 1811: שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע כי הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים, כולן או מקצתן, לא יחולו על עובד זר ... או שיחולו עליהם באופן חלקי
-- The power has been exercised: the Wikisource note at line 1812 records the
-- Income Tax (Credits for a Foreign Worker) Regulations 5775-2014. They can
-- only take credits away ("לא יחולו", "באופן חלקי"), so they matter only
-- where a section would otherwise give a foreign worker points; there the
-- rule refuses. Where the section gives nothing anyway, the answer stands.
@ref ITO s 48A, lines 1810-1812 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 34 — Credit for an Israeli resident`
-- line 1569: סעיף 34: זיכוי לתושב ישראל
-- line 1570: בחישוב המס של יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי.

@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 34 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year; reads residence under s 1 only, not s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `section 34, as written, applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1976. (0.3.0) It reads fork F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34, as written, applies to` p MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` p
    AND "שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס" ... `the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p

@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 34 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `section 34 applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1976. (0.3.0) It reads fork F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34 applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 34, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 34, as written, applies to` p
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` p AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי" — two credit points shall be taken into account.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 34 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1976. (0.3.0) It reads fork F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 34 for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 34 applies to` p
    THEN 2
    ELSE 0

§§ `Section 36 — Credit for travel to the place of earning`
-- line 1593: סעיף 36: זיכוי בעד נסיעה למקום ההשתכרות
-- line 1594: בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה.
--
-- The heading speaks of travel to the place of earning; the sentence imposes
-- no condition of earning or travel. Encoded as the sentence reads (fork F2).
-- "יחיד תושב ישראל" carries no "in the tax year"; read as the same
-- residence-for-the-tax-year that s 34 names (fork F3).

@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year; reads residence under s 1 only, not s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `section 36, as written, applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1978. (0.3.0) It reads forks F2 (every resident individual) and F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36, as written, applies to` p MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` p
    AND "תושב ישראל" ... `the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` p

@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `section 36 applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1978. (0.3.0) It reads forks F2 (every resident individual) and F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36 applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 36, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 36, as written, applies to` p
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` p AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` p
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- "תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה" — a quarter of a credit point
-- shall be taken into account, as a travel credit.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1978. (0.3.0) It reads forks F2 (every resident individual) and F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36 for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 36 applies to` p
    THEN 1/4
    ELSE 0

§§ `Section 36A — Credit for a woman`
-- line 1596: סעיף 36א: זיכוי לאשה
-- line 1597: בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי.
--
-- The sentence has one limb, "אשה". It does not say "תושב ישראל", as ss 34
-- and 36 beside it do, and s 48 does not list it among the sections it
-- extends to non-residents. Encoded as the sentence reads: residence is not
-- a condition (fork F1).

@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36A as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year; the year-aware rules use it after their own year check. For a named tax year use `section 36A applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1997. (0.3.0) It reads fork F1 (no residence condition), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A, as written, applies to` p MEANS
    "של אשה" ... `the person is a woman` p

-- s 48 does not reach s 36A, so only s 48A can change the answer.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36A as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year and applies s 48A's refusal in every year. For a named tax year use `section 36A applies in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1997. (0.3.0) It reads fork F1 (no residence condition), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A applies to` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 36A, as written, applies to` p AND `the person is a foreign worker` p
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE `section 36A, as written, applies to` p

-- "תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי" — half a credit point shall be taken into account.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of s 36A as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year and applies s 48A's refusal in every year. For a named tax year use `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1997. (0.3.0) It reads fork F1 (no residence condition), as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36A for` p MEANS
    IF   `section 36A applies to` p
    THEN 1/2
    ELSE 0

§§ `Aggregates the Ordinance names`

-- line 4864: מסכום נקודות הזיכוי שעל פי סעיפים 34 ו־36
-- s 134A(2) (a power to exempt from filing a return, outside this row) names
-- this aggregate, so it is provided under that name.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of ss 34 and 36 as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 1976 (s 34) or 1978 (s 36). (0.3.0) It reads forks F2 and F4 as above, as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; named in s 134A(2), line 4864
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` p MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 for` p

-- The whole of this row's slice. NOT the person's total credit points.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of ss 34, 36 and 36A as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f). For a named tax year use `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before its sections' limits (1976, 1978, 1997). (0.3.0) It reads forks F1, F2 and F4 as above, as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 for` p
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36A for` p

-- The same points as an amount of money, at the year's indexed value of a
-- credit point (s 33A; the value is an input, see ito-s33a-credit-point.l4).
-- (0.2.0) This was the row's @export in 0.1.0. It takes no tax year and cannot
-- see s 3A(f), so the @export moved to its year-aware twin at the end of the
-- module (`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in
-- the tax year of`). This rule is kept, unchanged, for the tests that use it.
@desc Year-free (0.2.0): answers on the text of ss 33A, 34, 36 and 36A as it now stands (the consolidation retrieved 2026-10-06) and does not check the tax year, applies s 48A's refusal in every year and cannot see s 3A(f); it was the @export until 0.1.0. For a named tax year use the @export, `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of`, which refuses a year before 2005 (s 33A) or a section's own limit. (0.3.0) It reads forks F1, F2 and F4 as above, as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did; the year-aware points rules decline by default where the text does not decide (Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08).
@ref ITO s 33A, line 1563; ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597
GIVEN p                               IS A Person  @desc the taxpayer: an individual (with residence, sex, Area-residence and foreign-worker facts) or a body of persons
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER  @desc NIS; the s 33A amount as indexed under s 120B for the tax year (2,904 for 2025 per the Israel Tax Authority)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the amount of` (`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` p) `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point`

§§ `The tax years the deposited text governs (0.2.0)`
-- The deposited source is one text, the Ordinance as consolidated at
-- retrieval on 2026-10-06. Each section's heading carries the consolidation's
-- list of the Laws that amended it. For the sections the year-aware rules
-- rest on, the last entry, its Hebrew year, and (counting that year's
-- entries in the list of amending Laws at line 5, as rows IL-02 and IL-08 do)
-- the Law it names:
--   s 34  (line 1569) ... תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2   5735, Sept 1974 - Sept 1975: Amendment No. 22, Sefer HaChukim 5735 p. 168
--   s 36  (line 1593) ... תשל״ה־2, תשל״ז־4   5737, Sept 1976 - Sept 1977: Amendment No. 28, Sefer HaChukim 5737 p. 318
--   s 36A (line 1596) ... תשל״ה־2, תשנ״ו     5756, Sept 1995 - Sept 1996: the Arrangements Law, Sefer HaChukim 5756 p. 24
--   s 3A  (line 453)  ... תשס״ב־9, תשע״ו־22  5776, Sept 2015 - Oct 2016: not identified (the count is ambiguous in that year)
--   s 33A (line 1561) see ito-s33a-credit-point.l4: 5764, first tax year 2005
-- None of these Laws is deposited, so no commencement is known here.
--
-- The rule taken (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md version 0.2.0): the deposited
-- text of a section governs a tax year that begins after the Hebrew year of
-- its last listed amendment has ended. For an earlier tax year the text may
-- differ, and the year-aware rule refuses. This can refuse a year the
-- amendment already governed; it never answers a year the amendment might
-- not have reached, unless the Law deferred its own commencement past the
-- next 1 January, which is not checked. A tax year after 2026 is answered on
-- the text as it stood at retrieval, a projection.

@ref ITO s 34, amendment list at line 1569, last entry תשל״ה־2 (Hebrew year 5735, ended September 1975)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year the deposited text of section 34 governs` MEANS 1976

@ref ITO s 36, amendment list at line 1593, last entry תשל״ז־4 (Hebrew year 5737, ended September 1977)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year the deposited text of section 36 governs` MEANS 1978

@ref ITO s 36A, amendment list at line 1596, last entry תשנ״ו (Hebrew year 5756, ended September 1996)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year the deposited text of section 36A governs` MEANS 1997

@ref ITO s 3A, amendment list at line 453, last entry תשע״ו־22 (Hebrew year 5776, ended October 2016)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year the deposited text of section 3A governs` MEANS 2017

@ref ITO s 34, amendment list at line 1569, last entry תשל״ה־2; the text before that amendment is not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976"

@ref ITO s 36, amendment list at line 1593, last entry תשל״ז־4; the text before that amendment is not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978"

@ref ITO s 36A, amendment list at line 1596, last entry תשנ״ו; the text before that amendment is not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997"

@ref ITO s 3A, amendment list at line 453, last entry תשע״ו־22; the text before that amendment is not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding does not hold the text of section 3A for a tax year before 2017` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 3A for a tax year before 2017"

-- Section 48A, dated from its enactment. s 48A (line 1811) is a power, and
-- its heading (line 1810) lists one amending Law, תשס״ג־3: the Law that
-- enacted it, of the Hebrew year 5763, which ran from 7 September 2002 to
-- September 2003. Counting that year's entries at line 5 (errata included,
-- as the citations of תשל״ו־5 and תשס״ג־4 elsewhere in the headings show the
-- consolidation counts them), the third is
--     חוק ההסדרים במשק המדינה (תיקוני חקיקה להשגת יעדי התקציב והמדיניות הכלכלית לשנת הכספים 2003)
-- at Sefer HaChukim 5763 p. 189, not deposited, so its date within 5763 is
-- not known here. From tax year 2002, the first that 5763 overlaps, s 48A
-- may have stood, and whatever regulations were in force under it that year
-- are not encoded; so from 2002 the year-aware rules refuse wherever s 48A
-- could take a credit away. Before 2002 s 48A did not exist and could take
-- nothing, so the section's own answer stands, within its own year limit.
--
-- The lead's choice (2026-10-08, assumed, not ruled), made on this agent's
-- objection to the first choice, which dated the refusal from tax year 2014
-- by the Regulations of 5775-2014 that the consolidation's note records:
-- line 1812: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (זיכויים לעובד זר), התשע״ה–2014.
-- A note is not law, and naming those Regulations does not say there was no
-- earlier instrument, so it cannot license full points for 2002 to 2013.
@ref ITO s 48A, amendment list at line 1810, last entry תשס״ג־3 (Hebrew year 5763, from September 2002)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first tax year section 48A could reach` MEANS 2002

§§ `Reading a taxpayer in a tax year (0.2.0)`

GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A Person
`the taxpayer of` c MEANS c's `the taxpayer`

GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax year of` c MEANS c's `the tax year`

GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 48A could reach the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the tax year of` c AT LEAST `the first tax year section 48A could reach`

§§ `Section 3A(f) — an Israeli citizen in the Area, as if an Israeli resident (0.2.0)`
-- line 471: (ו) בכפוף להוראות סעיף זה, יחולו על אזרח ישראלי שהוא תושב אזור או פועל באזור, הוראות פקודה זו כאילו היה תושב ישראל, בשינויים המחוייבים לפי הענין.
-- "The provisions of this Ordinance shall apply ... as if he were an Israeli
-- resident": ss 34 and 36 are provisions of the Ordinance, so their residence
-- limb is met by such a person (fork F11). s 48 (line 1807) takes "אזור",
-- "תושב אזור" and "אזרח ישראלי" from s 3A, and reaches only those Area
-- residents who are NOT Israeli citizens: the two sections divide the Area's
-- residents between them.
--
-- An individual entered as both an Israeli citizen in the Area (a s 3A(f)
-- fact) and a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen (the s 48
-- fact) is described by facts that contradict each other, and the two
-- sections would answer differently, so the rule refuses and says so.

@ref ITO s 3A(f), line 471; s 3A(a), lines 455-461; s 48, line 1807
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the facts say the taxpayer both is and is not an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` MEANS
    REFUSE "the facts say the taxpayer both is and is not an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)"

@ref ITO s 3A(f), line 471
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3A(f), as written, reaches the taxpayer in` c MEANS
        "אזרח ישראלי שהוא תושב אזור" ... c's `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area`
    OR  "או פועל באזור" ... c's `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`

@ref ITO s 3A(f), line 471; s 3A(a), lines 455-461; amendment list, line 453; s 48, line 1807
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3A(f) treats the taxpayer as an Israeli resident in` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `section 3A(f), as written, reaches the taxpayer in` c
               THEN FALSE
           IF `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` (`the taxpayer of` c)
               THEN `the facts say the taxpayer both is and is not an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)`
           IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 3A governs`
               THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 3A for a tax year before 2017`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

-- An Israeli resident under s 1 needs no s 3A(f), so s 3A's text, and its
-- tax-year limit, is consulted only for one who is not.
@ref ITO s 1 "תושב ישראל", lines 143-162 (an input); s 3A(f), line 471
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year of` c MEANS
    IF   `the person was an Israeli resident in the tax year` (`the taxpayer of` c)
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `section 3A(f) treats the taxpayer as an Israeli resident in` c

§§ `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4 (0.3.0)`
-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): where the text does not decide, one
-- named switch per fork, by default a refusal by name where the readings
-- give different answers to the question asked, every reading kept by name
-- and tested (NOTES.md, version 0.3.0 and the fork register). The three
-- switches below are the row's defaults; the year-aware points rules take
-- the three readings together as one record, and their names without
-- "under the readings" are at these defaults. The year-free rules over a
-- Person, and the BOOLEAN "section N applies in the tax year of" rules, read
-- as versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 did, and say so in their @desc.

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 36A on residence`
`section 36A — the reading this row takes on residence` MEANS
    `declined where residence decides section 36A`

@ref ITO s 36, lines 1593-1594; s 38(a), line 1603; fork F2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 36 on income from personal exertion`
`section 36 — the reading this row takes on income from personal exertion` MEANS
    `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`

@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; s 41(1), line 1691; fork F4; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year`
`sections 34 and 36 — the reading this row takes for part of a tax year` MEANS
    `declined for residence in part of a tax year`

GIVETH A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
`the readings this row takes` MEANS
    `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A — the reading this row takes on residence`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 — the reading this row takes on income from personal exertion`
        `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`             IS `sections 34 and 36 — the reading this row takes for part of a tax year`

-- The readings versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 took, silently: no residence
-- condition in s 36A, s 36 for every resident individual, and one residence
-- status for the whole tax year.
GIVETH A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
`the readings versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0 took` MEANS
    `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS `section 36A has no residence condition`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `section 36 for every resident individual`
        `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`             IS `one residence status for the whole tax year`

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"

@ref ITO s 36, lines 1593-1594; fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"

@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; fork F4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`sections 34 and 36 do not say what an individual who was an Israeli resident for only part of the tax year gets` MEANS
    REFUSE "sections 34 and 36 do not say what an individual who was an Israeli resident for only part of the tax year gets"

GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in` c MEANS
    c's `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year`

-- The same case with the individual's residence entered as TRUE, for the
-- points a year of residence would give (fork F4, apportioned).
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
`the same case, the taxpayer counted as an Israeli resident:` c MEANS
    `Taxpayer in a tax year` WITH
        `the taxpayer`                                                  IS `counted`
        `the tax year`                                                  IS c's `the tax year`
        `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area`              IS c's `an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area`
        `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`                   IS c's `an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area`
        `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS c's `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year`
        `the taxpayer's Israeli residence over the tax year`            IS c's `the taxpayer's Israeli residence over the tax year`
    WHERE
        `counted` MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `the taxpayer`
            WHEN `an individual` i THEN `an individual` (Individual WITH
                `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
                `a woman`                                              IS i's `a woman`
                `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS i's `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`
                `a foreign worker`                                     IS i's `a foreign worker`)
            WHEN `a body of persons` THEN `a body of persons`

-- Fork F4, for ss 34 and 36. Where the residence entered held for the whole
-- tax year, every reading gives the points for the year. For an individual
-- resident for m months only:
--   one residence status: the points for the year, as the residence entered says;
--   apportioned: 1/12 of a year of residence's points for each month, as
--     s 41(1) apportions ss 34 and 36 for a spouse married part of the year:
--     line 1691: ל־1⁄12 מנקודות הזיכוי לפי סעיפים 34, 36, 40(ב) ו־40ב כפול במספר החדשים
--   declined (the default) where the two differ, which is whenever the
--     section would give a year of residence anything.
@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; s 41(1), line 1691; fork F4
GIVEN c                                    IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      f4                                   IS A `A reading of sections 34 and 36 for part of a tax year`
      `the points for the year`            IS A NUMBER
      `the points for a year of residence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`for part of a tax year, in` c `, reading` f4 `, of` `the points for the year` `and` `the points for a year of residence` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the taxpayer's Israeli residence over the tax year`
    WHEN `the residence entered held for the whole tax year` THEN `the points for the year`
    WHEN `an Israeli resident for only part of the tax year` m THEN
        CONSIDER f4
        WHEN `one residence status for the whole tax year`
            THEN `the points for the year`
        WHEN `apportioned by the months of residence, as section 41 apportions`
            THEN `the points for a year of residence` TIMES m DIVIDED BY 12
        WHEN `declined for residence in part of a tax year`
            THEN IF   `the points for the year` EQUALS (`the points for a year of residence` TIMES m DIVIDED BY 12)
                 THEN `the points for the year`
                 ELSE `sections 34 and 36 do not say what an individual who was an Israeli resident for only part of the tax year gets`

§§ `Section 34, for a tax year (0.2.0)`
-- line 1570: בחישוב המס של יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי.

@desc The sentence of s 34 for the tax year: an individual counted as an Israeli resident (s 1, or s 3A(f)) by the residence entered for the year; no year limit, ss 48 and 48A not applied. (0.3.0) Reads fork F4 as one residence status for the whole tax year.
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; s 3A(f), line 471
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34, as written, applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` (`the taxpayer of` c)
    AND "שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס" ... `the taxpayer counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year of` c

@desc Whether s 34 applies in the tax year, with its year limit (1976) and ss 48 and 48A. (0.3.0) Reads fork F4 as one residence status for the whole tax year, as 0.2.0 did; for the points under the row's readings, which decline a part-year resident by default, use `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of`.
@ref ITO s 34, lines 1569-1570; s 3A(f), line 471; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, lines 1811-1812
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 34 applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 34 governs`
               THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 34 for a tax year before 1976`
           IF     `section 34, as written, applies in the tax year of` c
              AND `the person is a foreign worker` (`the taxpayer of` c)
              AND `section 48A could reach the tax year of` c
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 34, as written, applies in the tax year of` c
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` (`the taxpayer of` c) AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` (`the taxpayer of` c)
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (0.3.0) Under the readings r: only fork F4 reaches s 34.
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; fork F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r MEANS
    `for part of a tax year, in` c `, reading` (r's `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`) `, of`
        (IF `section 34 applies in the tax year of` c THEN 2 ELSE 0)
        `and`
        (IF `section 34 applies in the tax year of` (`the same case, the taxpayer counted as an Israeli resident:` c) THEN 2 ELSE 0)

@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; fork F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`

§§ `Section 36, for a tax year (0.2.0)`
-- line 1594: בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל תובא בחשבון 1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה.

@desc The sentence of s 36 for the tax year: an individual counted as an Israeli resident (s 1, or s 3A(f)) by the residence entered for the year; no year limit, ss 48 and 48A not applied. (0.3.0) Reads forks F2 (every resident individual) and F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year).
@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; s 3A(f), line 471
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36, as written, applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
        "של יחיד" ... `the person is an individual` (`the taxpayer of` c)
    AND "תושב ישראל" ... `the taxpayer counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year of` c

@desc Whether s 36 applies in the tax year, with its year limit (1978) and ss 48 and 48A. (0.3.0) Reads forks F2 (every resident individual) and F4 (one residence status for the whole tax year), as 0.2.0 did; for the points under the row's readings, which decline by default where those forks decide, use `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of`.
@ref ITO s 36, lines 1593-1594; s 3A(f), line 471; s 48, line 1807; s 48A, lines 1811-1812
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36 applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 36 governs`
               THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978`
           IF     `section 36, as written, applies in the tax year of` c
              AND `the person is a foreign worker` (`the taxpayer of` c)
              AND `section 48A could reach the tax year of` c
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           IF `section 36, as written, applies in the tax year of` c
               THEN TRUE
           IF `the person is an individual` (`the taxpayer of` c) AND `the person is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` (`the taxpayer of` c)
               THEN `section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (0.3.0) Under the readings r: forks F4 and F2 reach s 36. F4 first, as for
-- s 34; then F2:
--   every resident individual: that quarter point;
--   only with income from personal exertion: that quarter point if the
--     taxpayer had such income, else 0 (s 48 and s 48A cannot give or take
--     what the section does not give; the year limit still applies);
--   declined (the default) where the two differ: for a taxpayer without such
--     income whom the section would otherwise give anything.
@ref ITO s 36, lines 1593-1594; s 38(a), line 1603; forks F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion`
    WHEN `section 36 for every resident individual`
        THEN `under F4`
    WHEN `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion`
        THEN IF   `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in` c
             THEN `under F4`
             ELSE IF   `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 36 governs`
                  THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 36 for a tax year before 1978`
                  ELSE 0
    WHEN `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`
        THEN IF   `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in` c
             THEN `under F4`
             ELSE IF   `under F4` EQUALS 0
                  THEN 0
                  ELSE `section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point`
    WHERE
        `under F4` MEANS
            `for part of a tax year, in` c `, reading` (r's `fork F4, residence for part of a tax year`) `, of`
                (IF `section 36 applies in the tax year of` c THEN 1/4 ELSE 0)
                `and`
                (IF `section 36 applies in the tax year of` (`the same case, the taxpayer counted as an Israeli resident:` c) THEN 1/4 ELSE 0)

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; forks F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`

§§ `Section 36A, for a tax year (0.2.0)`
-- line 1597: בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי.
-- No residence limb (fork F1), so neither s 3A(f) nor s 48 reaches it; only
-- s 48A, dated as above, can change its answer.

@desc Whether s 36A applies in the tax year, with its year limit (1997) and s 48A. (0.3.0) Reads fork F1 as no residence condition, as 0.2.0 did; for the points under the row's readings, which decline a woman who is not an Israeli resident by default, use `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of`.
@ref ITO s 36A, lines 1596-1597; s 48A, lines 1811-1812
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 36A governs`
               THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997`
           IF     `section 36A, as written, applies to` (`the taxpayer of` c)
              AND `the person is a foreign worker` (`the taxpayer of` c)
              AND `section 48A could reach the tax year of` c
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE `section 36A, as written, applies to` (`the taxpayer of` c)

-- (0.3.0) Fork F1 read the other way: s 36A with the residence condition
-- of ss 34 and 36, met as theirs is (s 1 residence, or s 3A(f)). A man gets
-- nothing either way; a resident woman the half point either way.
@ref ITO s 36A, lines 1596-1597; s 3A(f), line 471; s 48A, lines 1811-1812; fork F1
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 36A, read with a residence condition, applies in the tax year of` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 36A governs`
               THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997`
           IF NOT (`the person is a woman` (`the taxpayer of` c) AND `the taxpayer counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year of` c)
               THEN FALSE
           IF `the person is a foreign worker` (`the taxpayer of` c) AND `section 48A could reach the tax year of` c
               THEN `section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (0.3.0) Under the readings r: only fork F1 reaches s 36A.
--   no residence condition: the half point as `section 36A applies in the
--     tax year of` gives it (0.2.0);
--   only to an Israeli resident: as the rule above gives it;
--   declined (the default) where the two differ: for a woman who does not
--     count as an Israeli resident in the tax year, whom the first gives the
--     half point (or refuses under s 48A) and the second gives nothing.
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `fork F1, section 36A and residence`
    WHEN `section 36A has no residence condition`
        THEN `with no residence condition`
    WHEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
        THEN IF `section 36A, read with a residence condition, applies in the tax year of` c THEN 1/2 ELSE 0
    WHEN `declined where residence decides section 36A`
        THEN BRANCH IF `the tax year of` c LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 36A governs`
                        THEN `this encoding does not hold the text of section 36A for a tax year before 1997`
                    IF `the person is a woman` (`the taxpayer of` c) AND NOT `the taxpayer counts as an Israeli resident in the tax year of` c
                        THEN `section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point`
                    OTHERWISE `with no residence condition`
    WHERE
        `with no residence condition` MEANS IF `section 36A applies in the tax year of` c THEN 1/2 ELSE 0

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`

§§ `Aggregates, for a tax year (0.2.0)`

-- line 4864: מסכום נקודות הזיכוי שעל פי סעיפים 34 ו־36
@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; named in s 134A(2), line 4864; forks F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r

@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; named in s 134A(2), line 4864; forks F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`

-- The whole of this row's slice for the year. NOT the taxpayer's total.
@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597; forks F1, F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r MEANS
         `the credit points under section 34 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36 in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r
    PLUS `the credit points under section 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r

@ref ITO ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597; forks F1, F2, F4
GIVEN c IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c MEANS
    `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`

-- The same points as an amount of money for that year. s 33A's own year
-- limit (2005) applies as well as each section's.
@ref ITO s 33A, lines 1561 and 1563; ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597; s 3A(f), line 471; forks F1, F2, F4
GIVEN c                               IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER
      r                               IS A `The readings of forks F1, F2 and F4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` `, under the readings` r MEANS
    `the amount of` (`the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `, under the readings` r) `credit points at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` `in tax year` (`the tax year of` c)

@export The amount in NIS of the credit points under Income Tax Ordinance ss 34, 36 and 36A for a taxpayer in a tax year, before ss 41 and 66 apply (not the taxpayer's total credit points), given the indexed value of one credit point for that year; refuses a tax year the deposited text may not govern, and declines by name where the text does not decide (a non-resident woman under s 36A, a taxpayer without income from personal exertion under s 36, part-year residence under ss 34 and 36; forks F1, F2, F4, Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08)
@ref ITO s 33A, lines 1561 and 1563; ss 34, 36 and 36A, lines 1570, 1594 and 1597; s 3A(f), line 471; forks F1, F2, F4
GIVEN c                               IS A `Taxpayer in a tax year`  @desc the taxpayer (an individual with residence, sex, Area-residence and foreign-worker facts, or a body of persons), the tax year as the calendar year in which it begins, the two facts of s 3A(f) (an Israeli citizen who is a resident of the Area, an Israeli citizen who operates in the Area), whether the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the year, and whether the residence entered held for the whole year or for how many months
      `the value of one credit point` IS A NUMBER                    @desc NIS; the s 33A amount as indexed under s 120B for that tax year (2,904 for 2025 per the Israel Tax Authority)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` MEANS
    `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A in the tax year of` c `at a credit-point value of` `the value of one credit point` `, under the readings` `the readings this row takes`
